# Exercise: i.+ (addition)
#
# The `i.+` operator adds two integers from the stack.
# (You can also write `i.add` - both forms work.)
# Seq also supports type-inferred `+` which works for both integers and floats.
#
# Stack effect: ( a b -- sum )
#
# Examples:
#   3 4 i.+    # Stack: ( 7 )  (explicit integer)
#   3 4 +      # Stack: ( 7 )  (inferred integer)
#   1.5 2.5 +  # Stack: ( 4.0 ) (inferred float)
#
# Your task: Add 10 and 25 to get 35.
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: test-add ( -- )
    # Your code here - push two numbers and add them
    0
    # Do not edit below this line
    35 test.assert-eq
;
